---
// OfflineProof (DEMO-04): the live half of "your document stays on your
// phone." The claim itself does not need this component to say it - on the
// home page HeroDemo already says both the claim and the airplane-mode
// invitation, and on the Sign/Redact tool pages the app bar's "On-device"
// badge and the invitation line beside the hero (see ToolPageLayout.astro)
// already cover that ground. Restating the claim a third time on the same
// page read as a pitch, not a fact - the block used to also render a `full`
// variant with the claim sentence for exactly that reason, and it was cut
// for stacking three statements of the same fact on one screen (DEMO-04
// direction change). So this component's only remaining job, on every page
// it appears on, is the part static copy cannot do: say so *while it is
// actually true*, via navigator.onLine plus the online/offline events. It
// renders nothing until the visitor is genuinely offline, and that is the
// moment the claim stops being marketing.
//
// It is pure progressive enhancement: with JavaScript disabled the element
// simply never gets text, which is the correct degraded state, and it never
// blocks or delays PDF processing - it only ever reads a browser flag.
//
// The <script> below intentionally has no `is:inline` - Astro's CSP
// auto-hashing only covers scripts that go through its bundling pipeline.
// See CLAUDE.md's CSP section and BaseLayout.astro's service worker
// registration script for the working pattern this follows.
---

<p class="type-body offline-status mx-auto max-w-[30rem] px-5 text-center font-semibold text-[var(--color-primary)]" data-offline-status aria-live="polite"></p>

<style>
  /* Collapses to nothing, padding included, in the common case (online, or
     before the script runs). The padding lives on the same element :empty
     hides, on purpose - an earlier version wrapped this line in a padded
     container and only hid the line itself, so the padding stayed behind as
     dead space even with no message to show. */
  .offline-status {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .offline-status:empty {
    display: none;
  }

  .offline-status:not(:empty) {
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const statusEl = document.querySelector('[data-offline-status]');

  function renderStatus() {
    if (!statusEl) return;
    statusEl.textContent = navigator.onLine ? '' : "You're offline right now. It still works.";
  }

  window.addEventListener('online', renderStatus);
  window.addEventListener('offline', renderStatus);
  renderStatus();
</script>
